		<label>Xiangying Type 38 M46</label>
		<description>Caliber: 6.5x50mmSR Arisaka. 5-round internal mag. Semi-Automatic.
		
The Xiangying is a self-loading rifle created by Wen Chengding of the Jin-Sui District Arsenal in 1946. The weapon is a gas-operated conversion of the Japanese Type 38 Arisaka rifle, with the gas piston being made from a spare Type 38 barrel attached to the right side of the rifle. A handful of examples were produced, though the weapons never saw any significant military service.</description>
